# Test: a BFD strict peer whose BFD session ALREADY EXISTS, created by a
# top-level `bfd { single-hop-session ... }` pinned entry to the same neighbour.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-bgp-bfd-strict -- the peer reads the BFD session's CURRENT
#            state rather than assuming Down. api.SessionHandle.Subscribe
#            delivers that state as its first value, marked Initial, and
#            Peer.startBFDClient seeds from it.
# PREVENTS:  the round-2 blocker. The pinned session is created at plugin
#            configure time, before any peer runs, so the peer's EnsureSession
#            finds the key and only bumps a refcount, and Subscribe used to
#            replay nothing. The peer therefore read Down until the session next
#            TRANSITIONED -- which for a stable session never happens -- and sat
#            in OpenSentBfdUpPending until the BGP hold timer dropped it to
#            Idle, then retried, forever. Nothing corrupted; the peer simply
#            could never establish, from a supported configuration.
#
# Method: a compiled driver launches ze with a pinned single-hop session AND a
# strict peer naming the same address. The peer's remote address completes no
# TCP handshake, so BGP never reaches Established, and the assertion is not
# about establishment: it is that the BFD wiring runs to completion with the
# pinned session in place. `bfd service delivered no initial state` is in the
# REJECT list, so a Service that stops delivering the snapshot fails this test
# rather than silently returning to the guess.
#
# The state-level proof, that an already-Up session is read as Up and the
# KEEPALIVE is not withheld, is
# TestSessionBFDStrictProceedsWhenBFDWasAlreadyUpBeforeTheSession
# (internal/component/bgp/reactor/session_bfd_strict_test.go), and the
# forced-red proof of the snapshot itself is
# TestSubscribeReportsAStateAnotherClientAlreadyReached
# (internal/component/bfd/engine/subscribe_snapshot_test.go).
#
# MEASURED, 2026-09-09: this test DISCRIMINATES the snapshot. Disabling the
# enqueue in Loop.subscribe (internal/component/bfd/engine/engine.go) and
# rebuilding the daemon fails it with `configuration rejected: bfd service
# delivered no initial state`, and restoring it passes. An earlier note here
# said the opposite; that measurement had broken Loop.EnsureSession's refcount
# branch instead, which gives the peer a session of its own whose creation
# transition arrives on the channel, so the reject string never fires.
#
# WHAT THIS TEST STILL CANNOT SHOW. The pinned session here never comes up,
# because nothing answers BFD on 127.0.0.254, so a snapshot of Down and an
# assumed Down carry the same VALUE: what fails without the snapshot is the
# absence of any delivery, not a wrong state. The state-level proof against a
# session that is genuinely Up is the interop scenario
# bgp-bfd-strict-reload-speaker, where the speaker answers BFD, a SIGHUP reload
# adds the strict peer to an already-Up session, and removing the snapshot
# leaves the peer unable to establish.
#
# What this test also shows is the key collision: the pinned entry carries
# `local 127.0.0.1` so its api.SessionRequest.Key matches the peer's and the two
# share ONE session, which is RFC 5882 Section 4.4. Since
# api.SessionRequest.Canonical landed, a pinned entry that OMITS the leaf is
# derived onto the same key wherever an interface backend can name the link;
# this daemon has none (`bfd session identity: no interface backend`), so here
# the leaf is still what makes the two agree.

option=env:var=ze.bfd.test-parallel:value=true
# BFD listens on the RFC 5881 / RFC 5883 FIXED ports, so every concurrently
# running BFD test's daemon binds the same wildcard tuple. SO_REUSEPORT lets
# them co-bind and the kernel then hashes each datagram to one socket in the
# group, which is the kernel-global surface option=exclusive exists for.
option=exclusive:group=bfd-ports


cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/bgp-bfd-strict-pinned:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:pattern=bfd plugin running
expect=stderr:pattern=bfd session opened for peer
expect=stderr:pattern=strict=true
